{
  "dom_id": "step-e12956",
  "name": "Example: Solving a One-Step Inequality",
  "problem": "What is the solution to $7z \\lt -21?$",
  "worked_solution": "The variable $z$ is being *multiplied* by $7.$ To isolate $z$, we perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $7.$ Remember to perform the same operation on both sides.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7z & <-21 \\\\ \\frac{7z}{7} & <\\frac{-21}{7} \\\\ \\frac{7z}{7} & <-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $7$ from the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7z}{7} & <-3 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{7}z}{\\cancel{7}} & <-3 \\\\ z & <-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $z \\lt -3.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
